================================================================================
3. THIRD-PARTY SOURCE MATERIAL — not ours to license
================================================================================

Applies to: everything under data/, and any question or regulation text
reproduced in content/ or on the site.

  * Amateur radio examination questions are produced by the Question Pool
    Committee of the National Conference of Volunteer Examiner Coordinators,
    which releases each pool into the PUBLIC DOMAIN by explicit statement on
    its release page — for example, "The NCVEC Question Pool Committee hereby
    releases into public domain the 2024-2028 Element 4 Extra Class Question
    Pool." Separately, 47 CFR 97.523 requires each pool to be published before
    it is used. Questions are reproduced verbatim because a paraphrase would
    defeat their purpose as study material. The pool diagrams are published on
    the same release pages, under the same statement, as that pool's graphics.
    NCVEC is not affiliated with this project and does not endorse it.

  * Code of Federal Regulations text, FCC public notices, and FAA and NIST
    publications are works of the United States Government and are not subject
    to copyright protection in the United States (17 U.S.C. 105).

  * Manufacturer datasheets (Belden, Times Microwave) are consulted but NOT
    redistributed. Only the measured values are used, and facts are not
    copyrightable. The documents are fetched to a gitignored directory for
    verification and never ship with the site.

  * Paywalled standards (ASTM F3411, F3586) are cited for what they specify
    and never quoted.

Provenance for every source document — URL, hash, retrieval date, and the
basis on which it is stored — is recorded in data/sources/MANIFEST.yaml.
Third-party software notices are in THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md.

